WEBVTT

00:05.110 --> 00:06.860
Hey! Here comes the knight in shining armor!

00:06.860 --> 00:08.440
Make way!

00:13.240 --> 00:15.240
This is my declaration!

00:15.240 --> 00:19.370
I will repay the debt that weighs upon 
the thin shoulders of the traveling nun!

00:19.370 --> 00:22.770
And once she gains her freedom,

00:22.770 --> 00:26.250
I will profess my sincere affections 
for the traveling nun Holo

00:26.600 --> 00:28.540
and request her hand in marriage!

00:30.130 --> 00:32.680
Ms. Holo has told me about 
the hardships she has endured,

00:32.680 --> 00:34.840
as well as your treatment of her.

00:34.840 --> 00:40.260
I wish to use my status and assets 
to give her the wings of freedom.

00:40.530 --> 00:45.520
She may not quit being my traveling companion 
just because she's no longer in debt.

00:45.520 --> 00:49.070
Of course. But I'm confident!

00:50.090 --> 00:53.650
She may not seem like it, but Holo 
is still a traveling nun. Marriage is—

00:53.650 --> 00:57.490
I know that Ms. Holo isn't actually 
associated with any monastic order.

00:57.490 --> 01:00.240
As such, marriage is still possible.

01:01.390 --> 01:02.450
I see...

01:02.450 --> 01:04.210
According to the laws of Kumerson,

01:04.210 --> 01:09.420
when a woman is in debt, 
the creditor becomes her legal guardian.

01:11.420 --> 01:14.630
You'll accept this 
contractual knife, won't you?

01:18.060 --> 01:19.270
Mr. Lawrence.

01:20.900 --> 01:25.260
I'm not careless enough to 
sign a contract I have yet to read.

01:25.260 --> 01:26.600
Of course.

01:29.820 --> 01:31.610
One thousand Trenni silver coins...

01:31.870 --> 01:34.900
That is the amount that Ms. Holo owes you.

01:36.170 --> 01:40.410
The deadline for payment is tomorrow evening. 
I will be sure to have the money ready.

01:40.410 --> 01:42.830
One thousand Trenni silver coins paid in cash.

01:42.830 --> 01:46.960
No negotiations on discounts or payments
in installments. Is that acceptable?

01:47.250 --> 01:48.580
Of course.

01:51.810 --> 01:52.840
I accept.

02:00.850 --> 02:03.430
Then, let us meet here again tomorrow.

02:05.470 --> 02:07.300
Sorry for all the commotion.

02:07.300 --> 02:13.110
Well, my companion won't be swayed 
just because a man took her debt.

02:14.430 --> 02:18.540
Lawrence, two! Amati, four! Who'll place bets?!

02:18.540 --> 02:19.990
Ten Illaid coins on Lawrence!

02:19.990 --> 02:21.130
My bet's on Lawrence, too!

02:21.130 --> 02:21.960
Me, too! Me, too!

02:21.960 --> 02:23.990
Twenty on Lawrence for me!

02:36.130 --> 02:43.850
Spice and Wolf

03:56.130 --> 04:00.130
<b>Episode 16
Night of the Festival and Misaligned Gear</b>

03:59.100 --> 04:01.630
Looks like you've been dragged 
into something troublesome.

04:01.970 --> 04:03.080
Mr. Batos.

04:04.020 --> 04:05.730
How embarrassing.

04:05.730 --> 04:10.100
I believe Mr. Amati has a way 
to gather all the funds.

04:10.100 --> 04:10.850
Huh?

04:10.850 --> 04:14.030
Though, it doesn't seem to be 
a very admirable method.

04:14.660 --> 04:16.480
I won't tell you the details,

04:16.820 --> 04:21.970
since it wouldn't be fair to
Mr. Amati if I took your side.

04:21.970 --> 04:23.980
I just wanted to let you know.

04:23.980 --> 04:24.820
Why?

04:26.180 --> 04:31.290
Whatever the reason, a willing 
traveling companion is a happy thing.

04:31.730 --> 04:35.540
It's painful for any traveling 
merchant to lose that.

04:36.440 --> 04:40.000
So? You accepted such a contract?

04:40.000 --> 04:40.990
Yeah.

04:41.400 --> 04:42.380
Hey.

04:42.380 --> 04:43.630
What?

04:43.630 --> 04:47.300
What will you do if that boy hands you 
one thousand silver coins?

04:47.570 --> 04:53.350
Well, after calculating the amount 
you've used, I'll give the rest of it to you.

04:53.350 --> 04:54.980
Do not test me so.

04:54.980 --> 04:58.320
It's not fair that I'm the only one 
who always gets tested.

04:58.830 --> 05:02.650
If Amati fulfills his end 
of the contract, so will I.

05:02.650 --> 05:03.650
Oh?

05:03.650 --> 05:07.300
Of course, you'll be free of debt 
and can do as you wish.

05:07.300 --> 05:09.310
You are quite confident.

05:09.310 --> 05:10.530
It isn't confidence.

05:11.300 --> 05:13.590
It's just that I believe in you.

05:18.690 --> 05:20.100
Goodness.

05:20.100 --> 05:23.670
You were a lot cuter when you were clumsier.

05:23.960 --> 05:27.290
I feel like I've grown a lot myself.

05:29.270 --> 05:32.060
Does acting with composure make one an adult?

05:32.060 --> 05:33.210
Doesn't it?

05:33.210 --> 05:38.880
Keeping your composure after weighing the odds 
on a favorable gamble is mere cunning.

05:38.880 --> 05:41.900
That is not what it means to be truly mature.

05:43.390 --> 05:49.380
For instance, would not refusing to accept 
Amati's contract also be an admirable act?

05:49.380 --> 05:50.620
No, that's...

05:51.190 --> 05:53.380
I am sure you took a look around to determine

05:53.380 --> 05:56.010
whether it would be shameful 
to do so or not, right?

05:58.420 --> 06:01.670
Try to imagine how I feel about the situation.

06:01.950 --> 06:06.330
I cannot believe you even considered 
accepting such a contract.

06:06.330 --> 06:08.620
I wish to always be with Lawrence!

06:08.930 --> 06:13.680
Even if it is a debt, it is something 
that connects the two of us together.

06:13.680 --> 06:16.300
I could never accept such a bond to be broken!

06:16.300 --> 06:22.360
So, even if it may be shameful, 
I cannot accept that contract!

06:22.700 --> 06:23.750
What do you think?

06:24.420 --> 06:26.360
If I were told such a thing,

06:26.360 --> 06:29.300
my heart would be brimming with happiness.

06:29.300 --> 06:31.470
Sure, that may have been 
a more manly thing to do.

06:31.470 --> 06:34.450
But whether that's the more mature 
thing to do isn't certain.

06:35.550 --> 06:36.880
That is true.

06:36.880 --> 06:40.120
Such actions would overflow 
with reckless youth.

06:40.120 --> 06:43.340
Though the words would make me happy, 
it would also make me want to barf a little.

06:43.600 --> 06:44.800
Right?

06:45.060 --> 06:46.340
When you think about it,

06:46.340 --> 06:51.270
being both a good male and a good 
adult may be a contradiction in itself.

06:51.270 --> 06:53.600
A good male has a childish side to him.

06:55.130 --> 06:57.470
A good adult is cowardly.

06:59.080 --> 07:03.980
What would the Wise Wolf Holo do 
as both a good woman and good adult?

07:03.980 --> 07:06.520
I would accept with a smile.

07:06.520 --> 07:09.740
Of course, once I accept the
contract and return to the inn...

07:09.740 --> 07:13.490
I would quietly come
forward—silently, like this—

07:14.050 --> 07:15.530
and lower my eyes.

07:23.980 --> 07:27.130
Well, you are a rather good merchant.

07:27.650 --> 07:32.280
I am sure you will take various 
measures behind the scenes.

07:35.070 --> 07:36.930
You want me to take you to the festival?

07:37.210 --> 07:39.560
You are a merchant that would 
not hesitate to use bribery

07:39.560 --> 07:41.160
to ensure a contract, are you not?

07:43.820 --> 07:46.770
Should you be walking around 
with the beauty in question?

07:46.770 --> 07:52.020
If I keep her cooped up in the inn, it'll really 
seem like I've shackled her with debt.

07:52.020 --> 07:55.070
That's what Mr. Lawrence is saying.

07:55.070 --> 07:56.290
What's the truth?

07:56.290 --> 07:58.090
The truth?

07:58.090 --> 08:02.040
I am shackled by an enormous amount of debt.

08:02.350 --> 08:07.840
The chain is so heavy it would be impossible 
for me to escape or see a bright future!

08:08.240 --> 08:10.920
If you remove this chain for me,

08:10.920 --> 08:14.590
I would gladly be buried in your wheat flour.

08:17.430 --> 08:19.550
No wonder Amati fell for you.

08:19.550 --> 08:23.040
Looks like Lawrence is 
the one who's shackled here.

08:24.030 --> 08:25.500
I've looked into it.

08:25.500 --> 08:27.310
Oh! Good job. How was it?

08:27.960 --> 08:30.840
Yes, um...

08:33.030 --> 08:34.280
So, how was it?

08:34.280 --> 08:34.990
Y-Yes!

08:35.400 --> 08:38.980
Two hundred Illaid was 
recorded in the tax ledgers.

08:40.060 --> 08:44.750
That means that Amati should have about 
eight hundred Trenni worth of assets right now.

08:46.960 --> 08:51.450
I'm sure he has some secret savings 
and some money owed to him, too...

08:51.450 --> 08:52.760
The gambling parlors in town?

08:52.760 --> 08:55.710
There's only cards, dice, and rabbit races.

08:55.710 --> 08:58.230
There's a betting limit, too.

08:58.230 --> 08:59.900
It'd be impossible with gambling.

08:59.900 --> 09:00.840
That's right.

09:00.840 --> 09:02.180
Speaking of gambling...

09:02.180 --> 09:07.590
People are betting on what happens 
after the contract with Amati.

09:04.170 --> 09:06.680
This whiter one is higher quality flour.

09:06.680 --> 09:07.900
Then, this one?

09:07.590 --> 09:08.690
Afterwards?

09:07.900 --> 09:08.690
This one...

09:08.690 --> 09:14.570
If Amati succeeds in fulfilling the contract, 
there will be another challenge.

09:15.700 --> 09:20.590
You're currently at an advantage 
with a ratio of 1:2.

09:20.590 --> 09:23.770
Looks like I need to get 
a share from the bookkeeper.

09:25.250 --> 09:27.660
So, what's really going on?

09:27.660 --> 09:34.960
In this world, many questions are difficult to 
answer openly, even if there is an answer.

09:34.960 --> 09:38.680
For instance, the mixture
quality of this flour...

09:41.100 --> 09:46.730
Would you like to ask what I will do 
if my debt is cleared?

09:46.730 --> 09:49.110
No, no! Not at all!

09:50.740 --> 09:54.570
At this rate, it looks like we'll need
to keep an eye on him directly.

09:54.570 --> 09:56.120
How insidious.

09:56.120 --> 09:58.450
I'd like you to call it a battle 
behind the scenes.

09:58.450 --> 10:02.480
I'm sure that he has someone 
monitoring my movements as well.

10:02.480 --> 10:04.410
Well, I wonder about that.

10:04.680 --> 10:10.740
Amati believes that it's a dirty tactic to use 
the connection network of town merchants.

10:10.740 --> 10:11.630
Really?

10:11.630 --> 10:15.010
He was born as the third son of a rich family,

10:15.010 --> 10:18.970
but went out on his own because 
he didn't want to be kept in the house. {Note: In other words, kept as a useless pet/family member.}

10:19.500 --> 10:23.430
Since he was able to amass 
his current fortune all on his own,

10:23.860 --> 10:25.380
he's really self-assertive.

10:26.180 --> 10:28.980
I see. He's young, on top of that.

10:28.980 --> 10:30.090
Yeah.

10:30.090 --> 10:32.920
He pretty much only believes 
in his own eye for fish,

10:32.920 --> 10:37.320
his own mouth for sales, 
and the blessing of God.

10:37.570 --> 10:41.990
However, I'd never hesitate 
to use all my connections.

10:42.540 --> 10:47.330
I don't know about knights, but there's no 
whining about a battle between merchants.

10:47.330 --> 10:49.710
I totally agree.

10:50.120 --> 10:53.680
It would be nice to be attacked 
head-on once in a while.

11:00.040 --> 11:00.840
A blowing horn?

11:01.280 --> 11:03.740
Did you just hear a shepherd?

11:03.740 --> 11:04.840
Yeah.

11:04.840 --> 11:07.770
If you think so, too, it must have 
really been a blowing horn.

11:08.180 --> 11:10.920
Do you think the shepherd girl is here?

11:11.500 --> 11:14.760
Even if she was, she wouldn't be 
blowing a horn anymore.

11:14.760 --> 11:16.990
She should be a tailor by now.

11:18.070 --> 11:21.980
If you do not get shaken, it seems as though 
I am trying to draw your attention.

11:21.980 --> 11:23.930
That makes me extremely delighted.

11:23.930 --> 11:26.120
So much so that I'm scared of 
what's to come later.

11:29.050 --> 11:32.000
It is the best freshly fried!

11:33.970 --> 11:35.000
I see.

11:35.000 --> 11:37.630
That horn was to signal 
the beginning of the festival.

11:38.090 --> 11:39.280
Shall we go?

11:39.880 --> 11:42.380
It is boring to just eat.

11:51.390 --> 11:52.600
I cannot see.

11:53.740 --> 11:54.480
Holo.

11:54.480 --> 11:55.550
This way.

12:06.830 --> 12:08.600
What an excellent view!

12:08.600 --> 12:11.000
We have to thank Amati for this.

12:41.650 --> 12:42.720
What is next?!

13:03.170 --> 13:04.600
Heave-ho!

13:16.210 --> 13:17.350
There!

13:25.170 --> 13:27.060
Come on, now! Line up!

13:47.160 --> 13:48.970
Let us join the dance!

13:53.540 --> 13:54.470
Okay.

13:54.720 --> 13:58.060
Just take care not to step on my feet.

14:00.300 --> 14:01.440
I'll try my best.

14:11.830 --> 14:13.290
Where are we?

14:16.250 --> 14:18.420
Where is my drink?

14:18.990 --> 14:21.380
Go to sleep so you can drink more tomorrow.

14:41.560 --> 14:43.360
This letter is for you.

14:43.360 --> 14:46.500
Also, Mr. Marc asks you to go 
visit his shop as soon as possible.

14:47.250 --> 14:48.070
As soon as possible?

14:48.360 --> 14:49.270
Good-bye.

14:51.260 --> 14:52.670
It's from Ms. Diana...

14:58.240 --> 15:00.290
Sorry, I'll step out for a moment.

15:00.290 --> 15:03.850
While holding a letter in your bosom 
that reeks of a female?

15:03.850 --> 15:05.900
She's a real beauty. Does it bother you?

15:05.900 --> 15:06.670
Fool.

15:07.180 --> 15:11.470
I went to see someone yesterday 
who knew a lot of northern legends.

15:11.470 --> 15:13.020
I even heard a story about you.

15:13.020 --> 15:13.720
About me?

15:14.020 --> 15:16.520
There's a legend about you 
in a town called Lenos.

15:16.520 --> 15:19.530
Wheat-Tailed Holou must have been you.

15:19.530 --> 15:21.260
I am not sure...

15:21.260 --> 15:22.970
I got some information about Yoitsu, too,

15:22.970 --> 15:25.810
since the story said 
which direction you came from.

15:26.350 --> 15:28.010
Is that true?

15:28.010 --> 15:30.110
It seems like you came 
from a forest east of Lenos.

15:30.110 --> 15:34.900
Yoitsu should be southwest of 
Nyohhira and east of Lenos.

15:34.900 --> 15:37.670
This letter probably has 
additional information.

15:38.250 --> 15:42.030
At this rate, we might be able to find 
the place faster than expected.

15:48.830 --> 15:51.420
I'm sure we'll find it if we spend 
half a year searching with my cart.

15:54.700 --> 15:55.470
Yes...

15:56.360 --> 15:57.020
Yeah.

15:57.810 --> 16:00.500
So, right now, I'm heading to Marc's place.

16:00.500 --> 16:04.260
While holding a letter in your bosom 
that reeks of a female?

16:05.580 --> 16:07.540
Fine, I'll leave it behind.

16:07.540 --> 16:09.190
You said she was a beauty?

16:09.190 --> 16:11.950
You can open and read the letter, if you want.

16:11.950 --> 16:14.020
If you can read, that is.

16:14.800 --> 16:16.040
Goodness.

16:16.040 --> 16:18.990
You go and play while asking me to help you?

16:19.310 --> 16:20.310
Sorry about that.

16:20.810 --> 16:26.100
Well, I made a lot of money 
this time, so I'll let it slide.

16:26.100 --> 16:28.420
You jumped on Amati's bandwagon?!

16:28.420 --> 16:31.670
Yeah, I made a lot of easy money.

16:33.390 --> 16:35.720
I was able to find out his method 
after you told me that

16:35.720 --> 16:38.090
Mr. Batos had an idea of 
what he was planning to do.

16:38.090 --> 16:39.470
Is he dealing in jewelry?

16:39.470 --> 16:40.930
Close, but not quite.

16:40.930 --> 16:43.720
He's using something 
that's a far cry from jewelry.

16:47.600 --> 16:48.610
Pyrite?

16:48.610 --> 16:51.660
Oh? You've heard of it?

16:51.660 --> 16:57.300
No, I was thinking it would make good money. 
Does it have to do with the fortune teller?

16:57.300 --> 17:01.220
Seems so. Even though the actual 
fortune teller has already left town.

17:01.220 --> 17:02.080
Is that so?

17:02.510 --> 17:08.920
The official rumor is that the fortune teller's 
skills were so good the inquisitors were called,

17:08.920 --> 17:11.540
but the whole thing's pretty suspicious.

17:11.540 --> 17:13.020
I'm sure.

17:13.020 --> 17:14.910
It would've caused a huge commotion

17:14.910 --> 17:16.840
if people from the Church 
came to investigate in this town.

17:17.750 --> 17:22.270
The amount of pyrite the fortune teller 
circulated was unusually high.

17:22.640 --> 17:27.730
I'm sure he bought it in some other town 
and left after he sold it all here.

17:31.810 --> 17:33.440
How much do you think they cost right now?

17:33.690 --> 17:37.820
They're normally about ten Illaid coins, so...

17:38.450 --> 17:39.290
One hundred.

17:39.290 --> 17:41.030
Two hundred and seventy.

17:41.030 --> 17:41.880
No way!

17:41.880 --> 17:44.660
I'm sure the price will go up 
when the market opens tomorrow.

17:44.970 --> 17:48.580
All the women in town are
scrambling for them right now.

17:48.980 --> 17:52.300
But, for this? Two hundred and seventy?!

17:52.300 --> 17:56.610
The women are all asking rich merchants 
or farmers to buy this miracle stone for them

17:56.610 --> 18:01.070
and competing with each other 
on how much was spent.

18:01.070 --> 18:05.350
The more women ask for it in sweet 
voices, they higher they rise in price.

18:05.610 --> 18:08.840
The profits aren't at the level 
of percent of cost.

18:08.840 --> 18:10.730
It's at how many times 
or tens of times of the cost.

18:10.730 --> 18:15.500
I dabbled in the matter a bit and I've 
already made about three hundred Illaid.

18:17.390 --> 18:19.920
How much has this spread?

18:19.920 --> 18:22.730
Everyone knew about it by morning.

18:22.730 --> 18:25.250
Around the time you were
 dancing with the princess,

18:25.250 --> 18:28.620
there was a huge uproar 
at the stone merchant shops.

18:28.910 --> 18:31.820
I can't believe I didn't notice 
such a profitable deal.

18:31.820 --> 18:33.380
I'm a failure as a merchant.

18:33.380 --> 18:35.640
Hey, it's still not over.

18:35.640 --> 18:38.560
Merchants planning to sell the stuff 
have been running around and buying it all up.

18:38.560 --> 18:40.640
The price can only rise.

18:41.320 --> 18:43.130
Then, do you think I still have a chance?

18:43.130 --> 18:44.670
Yeah, that's the spirit.

18:44.670 --> 18:50.400
Worst case scenario, don't you need to 
save money to find yourself a new princess?

18:51.660 --> 18:57.100
Then, let me buy this pyrite from you 
with the money you owe me for the nails.

18:58.450 --> 19:04.030
Jokes aside, I heard that Amati 
has been making a huge killing in profits.

19:04.030 --> 19:07.750
I'm sure he'll prepare a thousand Trenni silver 
coins just like he stated in the contract.

19:08.120 --> 19:10.580
Will your princess be all right?

19:10.580 --> 19:12.630
I told you that there's nothing to worry about.

19:13.820 --> 19:17.720
Amati doesn't know, but Holo is 
traveling with a destination in mind.

19:17.720 --> 19:19.630
I'm the one going along with her.

19:20.000 --> 19:24.670
I'll raise our traveling funds 
with the thousand silver coins and pyrite!

20:02.850 --> 20:04.920
You can read...

20:06.570 --> 20:08.770
Hey, what should I do?

20:09.510 --> 20:13.390
I no longer have a place to return to.

20:16.120 --> 20:17.550
What should I do?

20:17.550 --> 20:21.350
They're just old legends. 
A lot of them are false.

20:21.350 --> 20:22.740
False?

20:22.740 --> 20:23.790
That's right.

20:23.790 --> 20:26.560
When a new king or people take over an area,

20:26.560 --> 20:29.100
they often create 
fake stories to cover things up.

20:31.050 --> 20:34.540
Then, why did you keep this from me?

20:35.190 --> 20:37.580
I wanted to find the right time to tell you.

20:37.580 --> 20:40.500
I know that it's a really 
sensitive topic, so...

20:41.950 --> 20:45.890
It must have been amusing 
to watch me grow so excited,

20:45.890 --> 20:48.070
completely oblivious to the truth.

20:48.660 --> 20:50.420
Holo! Calm down!

20:50.420 --> 20:52.390
I am! I am calm.

20:52.930 --> 20:56.270
You knew what happened 
to Yoitsu long ago, did you not?

20:57.240 --> 20:59.360
I see. Of course.

20:59.360 --> 21:03.360
You must have known. 
Now many things make sense.

21:05.570 --> 21:09.490
After all, you love pathetic 
and weak little lambs.

21:10.020 --> 21:11.120
What did you think of me,

21:11.120 --> 21:15.210
who wanted to return to a home 
that had long since disappeared?

21:15.720 --> 21:20.290
Was I foolishly cute? Pathetically adorable?

21:20.290 --> 21:23.250
Is that not why you allowed me 
to be selfish and treated me so kindly?!

21:23.250 --> 21:23.970
Holo...

21:24.990 --> 21:29.340
Did you tell me to go back to Nyohhira alone 
because you have grown tired of me?!

21:29.940 --> 21:32.050
Do you really think so?

21:32.050 --> 21:34.220
Yes! I do!

21:41.500 --> 21:44.570
Once again, I am alone.

21:44.850 --> 21:48.020
Wh-Wh-What should I do?

21:48.020 --> 21:52.620
No one is waiting for my return 
any longer. Nowhere.

21:52.620 --> 21:55.540
I am now alone...

21:57.190 --> 21:58.480
I'm here.

22:01.140 --> 22:03.140
What are you to me?!

22:03.140 --> 22:05.670
No, what am I to you?!

22:10.700 --> 22:11.790
No...

22:12.310 --> 22:14.640
I do not wish to be alone again...

22:17.580 --> 22:21.430
Hey, Lawrence, will you make love to me?

22:22.310 --> 22:25.990
I am currently in the form of a human.

22:26.530 --> 22:29.240
Should it not be possible to do so?

22:29.520 --> 22:31.170
I am now alone.

22:31.170 --> 22:34.320
But if I have a child, there will be 
two of us, right? Lawrence?!

22:34.320 --> 22:36.370
Stop talking like that. Please!

22:39.500 --> 22:40.710
That is right!

22:40.980 --> 22:44.410
You are good-natured. 
I did not place any hope in you.

22:44.850 --> 22:47.720
However, it does not matter. I remember now.

22:48.190 --> 22:53.220
There is... That is right, 
there is someone who loves me.

22:53.970 --> 22:57.680
This is why you were never 
flustered from the start, right?

22:58.080 --> 23:01.440
You thought a thousand silver coins 
would be worth the loss, did you not?!

23:05.940 --> 23:06.530
Holo.

23:08.100 --> 23:09.030
I am sorry.

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Episode 17

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Traveling Merchant's Shallow Thinking
and Town Merchant's Signboard

23:45.860 --> 23:49.820
